message: Please cite the paper; this repository supplies its source.
type: software
title: "One noisy cellular automaton with an uncomputable noise diagram"
version: 1.4.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24147268"
date-released: '2026-11-13'
license: [CC-BY-4.0, MIT, Apache-2.0]
authors: [{"family-names": "Douglas", "given-names": "Seth", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"}, {"family-names": "Mghirbi", "given-names": "Nidhal", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6534-1118"}]
keywords: ["cellular automata", "probabilistic cellular automata", "noise", "ergodicity", "undecidability", "halting problem", "Gibbs measures", "noise diagram"]
abstract: "We construct one computably specified finite-alphabet, finite-range cellular automaton on Z^3 with computable disjoint nonempty rational rate windows. Throughout the nth window, uniform whole-symbol replacement is ergodic exactly when a fixed universal machine halts on n. Halting gives exponential full-symbol coalescence over all starts, with a fixed positive computable decay coefficient and an effective halting-dependent prefactor uniform on each window; nonhalting gives two stationary laws invariant under every spatial translation. A corner-deterministic chart, causal L-frame computations, history strips, private interval sensors and a packed wrong-gate boundary give the construction. Its fixed finite-range {0,1}-energy space-time interaction on Z^4 has computable rational inverse-temperature windows: halting is equivalent to uniqueness among all Gibbs measures and gives exponential weak spatial mixing in arbitrary volumes. Earlier results on Z^4, Z^5, Z^6 and Z^7 are retained. Lean verifies the stated original six-dimensional results; the three- and four-dimensional automaton results are not formalized."
